# Line endings are normalized to LF, in the repository and in the working tree.
#
# Without this file, and with core.autocrlf=false, whatever a tool happens to write is what
# gets committed. A script that rewrites a CRLF file with LF endings then turns a two-line
# edit into a whole-file diff, which hides the real change and makes the history useless for
# blame. `eol=lf` additionally keeps the working tree LF, so what is on disk is what is
# committed.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Hooks must stay LF to run under sh.
.githooks/* text eol=lf

# Expected output is compared byte for byte: CSV lines end in CRLF by design, and Parquet is
# binary. Never convert either.
testdata/** -text
